'''Barry Stephen Hill''' (January 26, 1953 - December 29, 2010) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[defensive back]] for the [[Miami Dolphins]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL).<ref>[https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/H/HillBa20.htm Barry Hill NFL & AFL Football Statistics - Pro-Football-Reference.com]</ref> He played [[college football]] for the [[Iowa State Cyclones football|Iowa State Cyclones]] and was selected in the fifth round of the [[1975 NFL draft]]. He enjoyed a successful rookie campaign with the Dolphins, winning the teams' Tommy Fitzgerald Award as the outstanding rookie in training camp as well as being named the Outstanding Special Teams Player.{{Citation needed|date=June 2023}}

==College==

Barry Hill was a three-year letterman in college, playing cornerback and safety for the Cyclones from 1972 to 1974.{{Citation needed|date=June 2023}}

Hill was generally regarded as the best athlete on the ISU campus after starring in football and basketball at Carver High School in Delray Beach, Fla. Hill turned down a basketball scholarship from Brown University.{{Citation needed|date=June 2023}}

